  "body": "**Found by:** the second review of PR #2659 (comment 6997335188, point F3). Related: #2597.\n\n**What happens:** the cover unions `band.center`. This can include a ring that `trim_ladder` drops from an emitted band. The review proved by reading and by a probe that this cannot make a later pass start too deep. But the invariant depends on that proof, not on the code.\n\n**Wanted:** add to `cover` only the rings that have levels after `trim_ladder`. Then the cover never claims material that no pass removed.\n\n**Done means:** the change is in, the tests of `contour_whole` and `contour_whole_new_outline` are green, and a test pins a band whose ring is trimmed away.\n\nClose this issue with a comment if the review fix of PR #2659 already includes the change.\n",
